# APML v2.0.0 - Lazy Loading & Instant Startup
# SSI Learning App
# Last Updated: 2026-07-19

spec lazy_loading_architecture:
  version: "2.0.0"
  status: "implemented"
  date: "2026-06-08"

  superseded_design_notice: |
    The original PriorityRoundLoader / SessionController / CyclePlayer
    "lazy loader" described by v1.0.0 was DELETED 2026-06-08. None of
    PriorityRoundLoader, SessionController, CyclePlayer, ThreadManager,
    RoundBuilder or PlaybackConfig exist in the tree any more. The
    belt-aware priority queue, course-end-detection loop and incremental
    SessionController methods (initializeEmpty/addRound/addRounds) are
    GONE.

    LIVE startup is now the "instant playback" path:
      composables/useInstantPlayback.ts  (bootstrap → round-map + cycles,
      localStorage-cached) feeding the player's rounds, with
      `const INSTANT_PLAYBACK_ALL = true` in LearningPlayer.vue so every
      course takes this path. The legacy upfront-load assembly is kept ONLY
      as a flag-off catch-fallback (try/catch around the bootstrap call in
      loadAllData); flipping INSTANT_PLAYBACK_ALL false is the escape hatch.

    Cross-reference the authoritative, code-traced write-up:
      docs/cold-start-and-playback.md  (the doc that wins on disagreement).
    The 4-phase cycle playback itself lives in
      playback/SimplePlayer.ts + composables/useCyclePlayback.ts + the
      RealAudioController class defined inside LearningPlayer.vue
    (not the deleted @ssi/core CycleOrchestrator/AudioController).

    Sections below are reconciled to that reality. Where a v1.0.0 concept
    has no live equivalent it is marked REMOVED rather than silently kept.

  description: |
    Instant startup (< 2s to first play) via a per-course round-map +
    on-demand cycle fetch, both localStorage-cached so a returning learner
    pays ~0 network to bootstrap. There is no longer a belt-by-belt
    background loading QUEUE: the round-map gives O(1) position lookup for
    skips, and audio is supplied by a rolling filler + IndexedDB cache (see
    apml/cache/audio-architecture.apml), not a round loader.
    Users can still only skip ONE belt ahead — but that's now enforced by UI,
    not by a loading priority queue.

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## DESIGN PRINCIPLES
  ## ==========================================================================

  principles:
    instant_play: |
      First play must happen in < 2 seconds. The critical path is:
      resolve resume position → fetch round-map (1 tiny query, cached forever
      per course version) → fetch ONE cycle (limit=1) → hand to the player.
      Warm caches (localStorage round-map + cycles, IndexedDB WAV blobs)
      collapse this to ~0 network for a returning learner.

    splash_floor: |
      Ready is gated by a DELIBERATE animation floor, not data:
      `MINIMUM_ANIMATION_MS = isReturnUser ? 300 : 2800` in LearningPlayer.vue.
      Return users get a 300ms minimum splash; first-ever visitors get a
      2800ms cinematic. When total-ready ≈ this floor, the floor is the gate.
      onMounted: `await Promise.all([loadAllData(), runAnimationTimeline()])`
      then `warmFirstKnownAudio()` then `setLoadingStage('ready')`.

    deferred_hydration_off_critical_path: |
      Belt progress, the adaptation engine, and Layer-1 listening hydration
      each cost a Supabase round-trip but NONE is needed for the first cycle,
      so they run fire-and-forget concurrently, off the critical path.
      Consumers are null-safe with defaults: getPauseMultiplier(legoId) ?? 1.0,
      belt computeds `?. ?? default`. (LearningPlayer.vue onMounted, ~L9971.)

    intent_probability: |
      Users can only skip ONE belt ahead — but this is now a UI constraint,
      NOT a loading priority queue. The round-map gives O(1) lookup of any
      round's start LEGO, so a skip is just a fresh bootstrap at that legoId
      (instantPlayback.getOrFetchRoundMap / setCurrentLegoId), with cycles
      fetched on demand. There is no longer a buildLoadingQueue ordering of
      next-round / next-belt / belt-by-belt; that whole algorithm was REMOVED
      with PriorityRoundLoader.

    graceful_course_end: |
      Course end is the final round-map entry — there is no per-seed probe
      loop to overrun, so the "detect once / suppress spam logging / clear
      queue" machinery of v1.0.0 no longer exists. The round-map simply has
      no entry past the last round.

    coalesced_boot_fetches: |
      On a COLD course switch, the SAME round-map / cycles GET is requested
      by several callers at once: prewarmInstantCaches (fire-and-forget on
      course select), the resume resolver's getOrFetchRoundMap, the mount
      bootstrap's round-map + cycles fetch, and — after any cache hit — the
      background revalidate. Before 2026-07-19 they raced: every one missed
      the not-yet-written localStorage cache and fetched cold, so one
      round-map + one cycles fetch became ×3 each and prewarm ADDED load
      instead of preventing it. useInstantPlayback.ts now routes every
      round-map / cycles GET through a module-level in-flight coalescer
      (`coalescedJsonGet`, keyed by URL, cleared on settle): concurrent
      identical GETs share ONE fetch resolving to already-parsed JSON (no
      shared-body hazard). A genuinely-later refetch — the intentional
      post-first-paint revalidate once the first has landed — still hits the
      network, so version-bump detection is preserved; only the duplication
      is killed. The shared fetch owns its own BOOT_FETCH_TIMEOUT_MS timeout;
      a per-caller AbortSignal still lets one caller stop awaiting (its boot
      timeout, or cancel() on unmount) without aborting the shared fetch that
      other coalesced callers depend on.

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## BELT SYSTEM
  ## ==========================================================================
  ## NOTE: thresholds below are still the live belt boundaries, but they no
  ## longer drive any loading priority (PriorityRoundLoader is gone). Belt
  ## logic now lives in useBeltProgress.ts and is hydrated OFF the critical
  ## path (see deferred_hydration_off_critical_path above).

  belts:
    thresholds:
      - name: "White"
        index: 0
        start: 1      # Seeds 1-7
        end: 7
      - name: "Yellow"
        index: 1
        start: 8      # Seeds 8-19
        end: 19
      - name: "Orange"
        index: 2
        start: 20     # Seeds 20-39
        end: 39
      - name: "Green"
        index: 3
        start: 40     # Seeds 40-79
        end: 79
      - name: "Blue"
        index: 4
        start: 80     # Seeds 80-149
        end: 149
      - name: "Purple"
        index: 5
        start: 150    # Seeds 150-279
        end: 279
      - name: "Brown"
        index: 6
        start: 280    # Seeds 280-399
        end: 399
      - name: "Black"
        index: 7
        start: 400    # Seeds 400+
        end: infinity

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## REMOVED: PRIORITY ROUND LOADER  (deleted 2026-06-08)
  ## ==========================================================================

  priority_round_loader:
    status: "REMOVED"
    former_file: "packages/player-vue/src/playback/PriorityRoundLoader.ts (deleted)"
    note: |
      The belt-aware buildLoadingQueue priority queue, the per-seed
      course-end-detection loop, the deduplicated error logging and the
      onRoundReady/onBeltReady/onError event surface no longer exist. The
      replacement (instant_playback below) needs none of it: position lookup
      is O(1) via the round-map and audio supply is a rolling filler + cache,
      not a seed-by-seed loader. Removal also documented in
      docs/cold-start-and-playback.md ("removed 2026-06-08; INSTANT_PLAYBACK_ALL
      = true means it was never instantiated").

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## INSTANT PLAYBACK  (the live startup path)
  ## ==========================================================================

  instant_playback:
    file: "packages/player-vue/src/composables/useInstantPlayback.ts"
    flag: "const INSTANT_PLAYBACK_ALL = true  (LearningPlayer.vue ~L104)"
    purpose: "Sub-second time-to-first-play via round-map + on-demand cycles"

    round_map:
      api: "GET /api/courses/:code/round-map  (api/courses/[code]/round-map.ts)"
      shape: "{ course_code, version, rounds: [{ r, legoId, seed }] }"
      cache: |
        localStorage, version-stamped, key prefix
        'ssi-instant-playback-roundmap-<courseCode>'. Position-independent, so
        cached forever per course version and reusable across course switches.
        version bumps on any LEGO/decomposition change → cache bust on read.

    cycles:
      api: "GET /api/courses/:code/cycles?from=:legoId&limit=N"
      wire_type: |
        BackendCycle (type: intro | debut | build | use | listening) — distinct
        from the atomic playback Cycle in types/Cycle.ts; the player converts
        each backend cycle into one or more atomic PROMPT/PAUSE/VOICE_1/VOICE_2
        cycles. Carries display_tiling (authored tiles) when present.
      cache: |
        localStorage, validated against the current round-map version on read,
        so a content edit that bumps the version evicts stale cycles.

    bootstrap_critical_path: |
      bootstrap(legoId?):
        1. Resolve start LEGO — resolveStartLegoId() (the enrollment's
           last_completed_lego_id via progressStore.getEnrollment) unless an
           explicit legoId is passed. null = fresh learner → round-map's first.
        2. Get round-map (cache hit = 0 network; cold = 1 tiny fetch).
        3. Fetch ONE cycle (limit=1) for the start LEGO.
        4. Return { firstCycle, mapVersion }; the caller (loadAllData) hands
           the rounds to SimplePlayer. Audio is the audio controller's job.
      For a returning learner with warm caches this is ~0 network. On any
      bootstrap throw the caller falls back to the legacy upfront-load path.

    prefetch_tiers: |
      Run DURING playback, never blocking:
        - prefetchTier1: rest of the current round's cycles (limit=15).
        - prefetchTier3: the next round's cycles.
      The old Tier 2 bulk presentation/listening prefetch was disabled
      2026-05-23 — that audio JIT-fetches at use time on
      audioCache.persistent.ensure + SW CacheFirst, with
      SimplePlayer.prefetchNextCycle warming the upcoming voices.

    inf_play: |
      bootstrapInfPlay(fromRound) is a parallel entry that manufactures a
      synthetic round-map for the infinite-play sequence (no real round-map
      equivalent), keeping main-loop bootstrap latency low.

    prewarm_on_switch:
      function: "prewarmInstantCaches(courseCode)  (useInstantPlayback.ts ~L265)"
      caller: "App.vue ~L272 (void prewarmInstantCaches(courseCode) on course switch)"
      purpose: |
        Warm the round-map (and position-0 cycles) localStorage caches for a
        course WITHOUT mounting the player, so the next mount's bootstrap() is
        a cache hit instead of two fetches — targets the slow course-switch.

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## ROUND HOSTING  (was SessionController — now SimplePlayer)
  ## ==========================================================================

  round_hosting:
    note: |
      SessionController + its incremental methods (initializeEmpty / addRound /
      addRounds) were DELETED 2026-06-08. The "SessionController path" phrases
      still scattered through LearningPlayer.vue comments now just name the
      instant-playback code path, not the deleted class.
    live_owner:
      file: "packages/player-vue/src/playback/SimplePlayer.ts"
      wrapper: "packages/player-vue/src/composables/useSimplePlayer.ts"
      surviving_method: |
        hasRound(roundNumber): boolean — now a SimplePlayer method (and
        re-exported by useSimplePlayer), the only piece of the old incremental
        API still present. The player owns the single <audio> element via the
        RealAudioController class defined INSIDE LearningPlayer.vue (~L5472)
        and warms the next clip via SimplePlayer.prefetchNextCycle().

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## COURSE DATA PROVIDER - LAZY METHODS
  ## ==========================================================================

  course_data_provider:
    file: "packages/player-vue/src/providers/CourseDataProvider.ts"

    audio_completeness_invariant: |
      All LEGO-loading and basket-loading queries filter out rows with any
      missing audio ID (known_audio_id, target1_audio_id, target2_audio_id
      all required NOT NULL). A cycle must never be presented to the player
      without all three audio IDs — partial-import courses (e.g. Greek
      2026-04) had NULL target audio that caused silent-play and
      circuit-breaker halts. The filter is applied at the query level in:
        - loadSessionItems / loadLegoAtPosition / loadLegoRange
        - getLegoBasket / getLegoBasketsForSeed / getBasketsBatch
      The diagnostic queries loadAllUniqueLegos / loadAllPracticePhrases
      (used only by CourseExplorer QA) deliberately do NOT filter, so
      admins can see broken rows.

    welcome_played:
      note: |
        CourseDataProvider also gates the course welcome via
        learners.welcome_played_at (per-LEARNER, course-agnostic; replaces the
        old per-course course_enrollments.welcome_played). It reads
        welcome_played_at and marks it through the JWT-gated service-role
        endpoint POST /api/welcome/played (idempotent — keeps the first
        timestamp). Welcome now plays once EVER per learner.

    lazy_methods:
      status: "VESTIGIAL — defined but no live callers as of 2026-06-08"
      note: |
        loadLegoAtPosition / loadLegoRange / getBasketsBatch still exist in
        CourseDataProvider.ts but were the seed-by-seed feed for the deleted
        PriorityRoundLoader; nothing in the tree calls them now (the round-map
        + /cycles API replaced them). The audio-completeness filter they carry
        is the same NOT-NULL-on-all-three-audio-IDs rule applied above. Kept
        for now; candidates for removal in a later tidy.

      loadLegoAtPosition:
        signature: "loadLegoAtPosition(seedNumber: number): Promise<LearningItem | null>"
        purpose: "Load single LEGO at seed position (formerly fast startup)"
        returns_null_when: "no row at position, OR row exists but audio incomplete"

      loadLegoRange:
        signature: "loadLegoRange(startSeed: number, endSeed: number): Promise<LearningItem[]>"
        purpose: "Load range of LEGOs (formerly belt loading)"
        deduplication: "Keeps first LEGO per seed_number"
        filters: "Only LEGOs with all three audio IDs populated"

      getBasketsBatch:
        signature: "getBasketsBatch(legoIds: string[]): Promise<Map<string, ClassifiedBasket>>"
        purpose: "Batch load baskets (one query instead of N)"
        filters: "Only practice phrases with all three audio IDs populated"

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## DATA FLOW
  ## ==========================================================================

  data_flow:
    cold_start_onMounted: |
      All in LearningPlayer.vue onMounted:
      1. await Promise.all([loadAllData(), runAnimationTimeline()])
         - loadAllData: resolve resume (getEnrollment) →
           instantPlayback.bootstrap() (round-map + first-round cycles; warm
           = 0 network via localStorage caches, cold = 2 tiny fetches) →
           build the player's rounds → apply saved cycle cursor.
         - runAnimationTimeline: enforce the splash floor
           (MINIMUM_ANIMATION_MS = isReturnUser ? 300 : 2800).
      2. await warmFirstKnownAudio()
      3. setLoadingStage('ready')
      Off the critical path, concurrently (fire-and-forget): belt progress,
      adaptation engine, Layer-1 listening hydration, loadGlobalLegoTexts,
      getCourseFinalLego, ensureMainLoopMap, courseBundle.load.

    course_switch: |
      App.vue calls prewarmInstantCaches(courseCode) so the next player mount's
      bootstrap() is a cache hit; the remount path logs [ColdStart] switch→ready.

    skip: |
      Skips use the round-map for O(1) position lookup, then re-bootstrap /
      setCurrentLegoId at the target LEGO with cycles fetched on demand —
      no priority-queue prioritize() and no waiting on a background loader.
      generateScript / useScriptCache still serve some skip + legacy INF-PLAY
      paths (see docs/cold-start-and-playback.md "Still live").

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## PERFORMANCE TARGETS
  ## ==========================================================================

  performance:
    note: |
      "Ready" is usually gated by the deliberate splash FLOOR, not by data —
      so first-play time is dominated by MINIMUM_ANIMATION_MS (300ms return /
      2800ms first-visit), not by loading. Compare the [ColdStart] and
      [LearningPlayer] Data loading complete logs to see which dominated.
    first_play:
      target: "< 2 seconds"
      gated_by: "splash floor when warm (data is ~0 network for returning learners)"
    next_round:
      target: "instant (cycles prefetched via prefetchTier1/Tier3 during play)"
    skip:
      target: "fast — O(1) round-map lookup + on-demand cycle fetch"

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## FILES SUMMARY  (live as of 2026-06-08)
  ## ==========================================================================

  files:
    live:
      - path: "packages/player-vue/src/composables/useInstantPlayback.ts"
        purpose: "Round-map + on-demand cycles bootstrap; prewarmInstantCaches"
      - path: "packages/player-vue/src/components/LearningPlayer.vue"
        purpose: |
          INSTANT_PLAYBACK_ALL flag, loadAllData/runAnimationTimeline cold-start,
          MINIMUM_ANIMATION_MS splash floor, RealAudioController class,
          cold_start telemetry, deferred off-critical-path hydration
      - path: "packages/player-vue/src/playback/SimplePlayer.ts"
        purpose: "Owns rounds + the single <audio> element; hasRound; prefetchNextCycle"
      - path: "packages/player-vue/src/composables/useSimplePlayer.ts"
        purpose: "Vue wrapper over SimplePlayer"
      - path: "packages/player-vue/src/composables/useCyclePlayback.ts"
        purpose: "4-phase cycle playback"
      - path: "api/courses/[code]/round-map.ts"
        purpose: "round-map endpoint"
      - path: "api/welcome/played.ts"
        purpose: "marks learners.welcome_played_at (welcome plays once ever)"
      - path: "packages/player-vue/src/providers/CourseDataProvider.ts"
        purpose: "Audio-completeness-filtered queries; welcome gate; vestigial lazy_methods"
      - path: "docs/cold-start-and-playback.md"
        purpose: "Authoritative code-traced write-up of cold start + playback (the doc wins)"

    deleted_2026_06_08:
      - "packages/player-vue/src/playback/PriorityRoundLoader.ts"
      - "packages/player-vue/src/playback/SessionController.ts"
      - "packages/player-vue/src/playback/CyclePlayer.ts (+ ThreadManager, RoundBuilder, PlaybackConfig)"
      - "packages/player-vue/src/composables/useSessionPlayback.ts (no longer present)"

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## VERIFICATION
  ## ==========================================================================

  verification:
    console_timing: |
      Watch for:
      - "[ColdStart] launch→ready Xms total ... | animFloor Z | returnUser ..."
      - "[ColdStart] switch→ready ..." (in-app course switch / remount)
      - "[LearningPlayer] Data loading complete in ..." (compare vs animFloor)
      cold_start telemetry event in player_events carries
      { isFreshLoad, mountToReadyMs, totalMs, animFloorMs, returnUser, guest }.

    warm_resume_test: |
      1. Play a course, then reload the dev URL.
      2. Returning learner → 300ms splash floor; bootstrap should be ~0 network
         (localStorage round-map + cycles, IndexedDB WAV blobs).

    network_throttling: |
      DevTools → Network → Slow 3G. First play should still be quick on a warm
      cache (caches collapse bootstrap to ~0 network); cold = 2 tiny fetches.

# =============================================================================
# VERSION HISTORY
# =============================================================================

version_history:
  v2.0.0:
    date: "2026-06-08"
    changes:
      - "Reconciled to instant-playback: PriorityRoundLoader/SessionController/CyclePlayer DELETED"
      - "useInstantPlayback round-map + on-demand cycles (localStorage-cached); INSTANT_PLAYBACK_ALL=true"
      - "Cold-start splash floor (MINIMUM_ANIMATION_MS 300/2800)"
      - "Belt/adaptation/listening hydration moved OFF the critical path (fire-and-forget)"
      - "prewarmInstantCaches on course switch; cold_start telemetry"
      - "Welcome plays once-ever per learner via learners.welcome_played_at + /api/welcome/played"
      - "CourseDataProvider lazy_methods marked vestigial (no live callers)"
      - "Cross-ref docs/cold-start-and-playback.md (authoritative)"
    implementation_status: "IMPLEMENTED"

  v1.0.0:
    date: "2026-01-27"
    changes:
      - "Initial lazy loading specification"
      - "PriorityRoundLoader implementation (REMOVED 2026-06-08)"
      - "Belt-aware priority queue (REMOVED)"
      - "Course end detection (no spam logging) (REMOVED)"
      - "Incremental SessionController methods (REMOVED)"
      - "CourseDataProvider lazy loading methods (now vestigial)"
    implementation_status: "SUPERSEDED"
    contributors:
      - "Tom Cassidy"
      - "Claude (AI Assistant)"
